cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  HemoFusion-Net: A Hybrid CNN-Transformer Network for Intracranial
  Hemorrhage Segmentation and Detection
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both this repository and the
  underlying PhysioNet CT-ICH dataset.
type: software
# Risha and Abu Kowshir Bitto contributed equally and are joint first authors.
authors:
  - given-names: Risha
  - given-names: Abu Kowshir
    family-names: Bitto
repository-code: 'https://github.com/kowshir-bitto/hemofusion-net'
abstract: >-
  A reproducible study on the PhysioNet CT-ICH cohort (75 patients, 2,814
  annotated axial slices, 318 hemorrhagic). HemoFusion-Net fuses a
  ResNet-34 CNN stream and a PVTv2-B1 transformer stream bidirectionally at
  every scale, decoding through an attention-gated U-Net with a multi-rate
  dilated bottleneck and deep supervision, and learns slice-level detection
  jointly with delineation. The pipeline produces the full model
  comparison, paired statistical tests, ablation grid and quantified
  Grad-CAM explainability analysis from a single command.
keywords:
  - intracranial hemorrhage
  - medical image segmentation
  - computed tomography
  - vision transformer
  - convolutional neural network
  - explainable AI
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: '2026-08-14'
